<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine BancoRio sells pension stake to Citicorp.</title>
<headline>Argentine BancoRio sells pension stake to Citicorp.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco Rio, controlled by Spain's Banco Santander said Thursday it had sold to Citicorp a 42.8 percent stake of its Pension Company Rio-Citi for $154 million.</p>
<p>Rio said in a letter to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange it had also sold to Citicard SA a 0.51 percent of pension fund Siembra AFJP SA for $1.85 million.</p>
</text>
